From 3cd09924f2912898860030b757129d00f06b8637 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rasheed <99349713+gitRasheed@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 02:08:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 57/61] NNS.caus / NNS.dep: remove dead and duplicated code

- Uni.caus: drop the unused xy <- NNS.norm(cbind(x, y), ...) (one
  extra normalisation per call) and the junk list(tau + 1) / named
  numeric(0) placeholders of the lag lists.
- NNS.caus_core: drop the 'recompute when equal or zero' blocks; they
  re-ran Uni.caus with identical deterministic inputs, doubling the cost
  on exactly those inputs.
- NNS.dep.matrix: drop the unused order / degree arguments and the dead
  'if (nrow(x) < 20) order <- 2'.
- NNS_dep.cpp: delete the exported but never called NNS_dep_matrix_cpp
  (and its workers), which used a different, mean-centred partition;
  RcppExports regenerated with Rcpp::compileAttributes (only those
  entries removed).

Results are unchanged: NNS.caus with tau 0, 1, 3, "cs", "ts", the
causation matrix, NNS.caus(x, x), NNS.dep matrices (sym and asym) and
NNS.reg(dim.red.method = "NNS.caus") are identical() before and after.
